description:
Cigna-Evernorth Services Inc. seeks a Software Engineering Advisor for the Plano, TX location responsible for Project Enablement & Process Optimization, including gap analyses to identify opportunities for process reengineering, enhancing user experience, and improving system performance.

 Responsibilities:
 • Develop application profiles, enterprise class structures, organizational layers, user access controls, and routing logic strategies.
 • Technical Governance & Risk Mitigation responsibilities include establishing and maintaining reusable technical assets and enforcing coding standards to align with functional and technical requirements.
 • Perform detailed risk assessments to support smooth change control and implementation processes.
 • Ensure effective communication of release changes to all stakeholders.
 • Lead requirement grooming sessions with business users and stakeholders.
 • Conduct technical feasibility studies to validate proposed solutions.
 • Prepare comprehensive design documents for Pega workflows, system integrations, interface specifications, exception\ handling, and failover/retry strategies.
 • Manage sprint planning activities including user story sizing, velocity estimation, backlog grooming, and task assignment.
 • Execute user story development, unit testing, defect resolution, and deployment activities.
 • Provide support for QA, UAT, release planning, production deployment, and post-go-live operation.
 • Hybrid work schedule

 Qualifications:
 • Bachelor’s degree in Computer and Information Science or related field and 5 years of experience in any Pega system architecture role with healthcare prior authorization.
 • All qualifying experience must include: creating responsive and intuitive user interfaces using Pega’s design system;
 • Building and customizing UI components like sections, harnesses, and layouts;
 • Applying consistent styling using skin rules and CSS overrides;
 • Ensuring compliance with accessibility standards and supporting multi-language interfaces;
 • Designing and implementing case types, stages, and processes;
 • Process modeling, including building workflows using flow rules, subprocesses, and decision points;
 • Implementing decision tables, decision trees, and declarative rules;
 • Data transforms, including managing data manipulation and orchestration logic;
 • Integrating with external systems using REST, SOAP, MQ, JMS, and other protocols;
 • Configuring data pages for data retrieval and mapping external data sources;
 • Implementing OAuth, SAML, and basic authentication for secure integrations;
 • Data modeling, including designing class structures, data types, and relationships;
 • Database configuration, including managing database tables, views, and optimizing queries;
 • Creating reports, dashboards, and leveraging Pega’s reporting capabilities;
 • Managing parallel development using branches;
 • Automating CI/CD pipelines for Pega applications;
 • Understanding rule resolution hierarchy and managing rule versions;
 • Using Pega unit testing, tracer, clipboard, and live UI tools;
 • Enterprise class structure, including designing scalable and reusable class structures;
 • Application and access control, including configuring application rules, access groups, roles, and privileges;
 • Creating and managing reusable assets like rulesets, components, and frameworks;
 • Analyzing and improving application performance using PAL, DB trace, and AES;
 • Agile methodologies, including sprint planning, backlog grooming, user story creation, and velocity tracking;
 • Collaborating with stakeholders to define and refine requirements;
 • Preparing design documents, release notes, and stakeholder updates.
 • Pega System Architect certification required






If you will be working at home occasionally or permanently, the internet connection must be obtained through a cable broadband or fiber optic internet service provider with speeds of at least 10Mbps download/5Mbps upload. 

